## Story Description
Implement the authentication layer and engagement management endpoints. The middleware validates the Supabase JWT on every protected route and injects the user's email into the request state. The engagements router handles creating and listing engagements for the authenticated user. This is the foundation that all other routers depend on for ownership checks.

## Acceptance Criteria
- Create file: backend/app/middleware/auth.py — class SupabaseAuthMiddleware(BaseHTTPMiddleware): validates Authorization: Bearer <jwt> header using python-jose jwt.decode() with SUPABASE_JWT_SECRET and algorithms=['HS256']; extracts email from payload['email']; injects request.state.user_email; returns JSONResponse(status_code=401) for missing or invalid tokens; skips validation for path '/health'
- Create file: backend/app/database.py — function get_engine() -> Engine: reads SUPABASE_DATABASE_URL env var; if set returns create_engine(url, pool_pre_ping=True); raises RuntimeError if not set. Function get_db_url() -> str: returns the env var value. Note: imports sys and adds repo root to sys.path so that 'from src.models.database import ...' works.
- Create file: backend/app/dependencies.py — async function get_current_user_email(request: Request) -> str: returns request.state.user_email. Async function verify_engagement_ownership(engagement_id: str, user_email: str, engine: Engine) -> dict: queries engagements table, returns engagement dict, raises HTTPException(403) if not found or owner_email != user_email.
- Create file: backend/app/routers/engagements.py — APIRouter with prefix='/api/engagements', tags=['engagements']:
-   GET /api/engagements — SELECT * FROM engagements WHERE owner_email = user_email ORDER BY created_at DESC; returns list
-   POST /api/engagements — body: {name, client_name, currency_label='AUD', engagement_title='Procurement Spend Diagnostic', llm_dry_run=true}; INSERT into engagements; returns created row including id
-   GET /api/engagements/{engagement_id} — returns single engagement; 403 if not owned by user
-   PATCH /api/engagements/{engagement_id} — updates any of: name, client_name, currency_label, engagement_title, llm_dry_run; 403 if not owned
- Register SupabaseAuthMiddleware and engagements router in backend/app/main.py
- Create file: backend/tests/test_engagements.py — uses pytest-mock or monkeypatch to mock JWT validation and DB calls: (1) POST creates engagement and returns id, (2) GET lists only engagements matching user_email, (3) GET unknown engagement_id returns 403, (4) unauthenticated request to /api/engagements returns 401
- Verify: pytest backend/tests/test_engagements.py -v — all tests pass

