## Story Description
Modify src/models/database.py so that get_engine() accepts either a SQLite file path or a full SQLAlchemy database URL (for Postgres). Add engagement_id columns to all five table definitions and update insert functions to accept engagement_id. The change must be 100% backwards-compatible: all existing tests that create in-memory SQLite engines must continue to pass unchanged.

## Acceptance Criteria
- Edit file: src/models/database.py — change get_engine(db_path: str) -> Engine to get_engine(db_url: str) -> Engine. Logic: if db_url starts with 'postgresql://' or 'postgresql+psycopg2://' use create_engine(db_url, pool_pre_ping=True); if db_url starts with 'sqlite://' use create_engine(db_url, connect_args={'check_same_thread': False}); otherwise treat as file path and prepend 'sqlite:///' as before.
- Edit file: src/models/database.py — add Column('engagement_id', Text, nullable=True) as the LAST column in: transactions_table, supplier_master_table, supplier_match_log_table, category_overrides_table, audit_log_table. nullable=True preserves backwards compatibility with existing SQLite data.
- Edit file: src/models/database.py — update insert_transactions(engine, records, engagement_id=None) to inject engagement_id into each row dict when provided and not None.
- Edit file: src/models/database.py — update insert() operations in any other insert helper functions (supplier_master, supplier_match_log, category_overrides, audit_log) to similarly accept optional engagement_id parameter.
- Edit file: src/config.py — add field database_url: Optional[str] = None to PathsConfig class (use from typing import Optional). When this field is set, the value takes precedence over db_path for constructing the SQLAlchemy engine URL.
- Verify: pytest tests/ -v — all 60+ existing tests pass with no regressions. This is the critical acceptance check.
- Verify: python -c "from src.models.database import get_engine; e = get_engine(':memory:'); print('sqlite in-memory ok')" — exits 0
- Verify: python -c "from src.models.database import get_engine; e = get_engine('sqlite:///test.db'); print('sqlite url ok')" — exits 0

